**Known for**: Twitter (co-founder); Block, Inc (Square, Cash App, etc);
nostr financial backer

Jack is the billionaire financial supporter of nostr, and donated $10M to the
nostr foundation, of which [Alex Gleason]($link.unsafeRef('gleason')) is a
member, and 14 BTC to "[Fiatjaf]($link.page('weird-guys').unsafeRef('fiatjaf'))"
directly.[[source]][0]

Jack joined the BlueSky board of directors in 2022, before pivoting to
nostr, leaving over the fact that Bluesky wanted to implement
centralized moderation tools.[[source]][1]
One of the main selling points of nostr is "censorship resistance", which
makes it particularly attractive for weirdos like those on this list who want
somewhere to say weird shit without getting moderated for it.

Jack also financially supports
[Andreas Kling]($link.page('weird-guys').unsafeRef('kling')),
[David Heinemeier Hansson]($link.page('weird-guys').unsafeRef('dhh')),
and [Evgeny Poberezkin]($link.page('weird-guys').unsafeRef('poberezkin')).

He chickened out of doing a keynote at FOSDEM in 2025 when I organized a
protest action against his presence there.[[source]][2]

